 lebai guided learning in Sarawak. They guided religious learning in the Sarawak context.", "Sabah. Formal education was still limited at that time. This refers to the past, rather than education today.", "Learning settings. In Sabah, study took place in surau, pondok and religious teachers’ homes. Religion, customs and education together helped shape community life."], "text": "Sarawak. Mosques and religious schools provided formal education. This description concerns Muslim communities. Foundational knowledge. Muslim communities studied Quran reading, Jawi writing and worship. Learning also included how to perform acts of worship. Teachers. Quran teachers, imams and lebai guided learning in Sarawak. They guided religious learning in the Sarawak context. Sabah. Formal education was still limited at that time. This refers to the past, rather than education today. Learning settings. In Sabah, study took place in surau, pondok and religious teachers’ homes. Religion, customs and education together helped shape community life."}